  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Brasfield and Gorrie reported $416M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Brasfield and Gorrie received 16 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $26M, and obligations were down 5.9% year over year. Brasfield and Gorrie concentrated obligations in Commercial and Institutional Building Construction, which accounted for $416M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $326M, followed by the Department of Defense with $59.6M and the General Services Administration with $20.7M. Historical obligations by fiscal year are: FY21 $178M, FY22 $154M, FY23 $679M, FY24 $587M, FY25 $442M, and FY26 $416M. Smaller NAICS markets in FY2026 to date include Engineering Services at $200K and Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction at $10K. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
